{"kind":"report","text":"Independent exact-head review: approved credential cleanup plan 003 revision 3 at 5c2ad4f67ad26b6212b5ea28fa2c7fc25c37f145. All seven artifacts inspected; the candidate differs from current main a6330262 only in the seven manifested paths. The immutable plan matches the adopted original; the added production Room integration test is the scope extension requested in f060871b. Both P2 findings in f060871b are repaired, and the earlier queue-blocking finding in 14739925 remains repaired.\n\nArchitecture: approved. Durable token duties remain separate from publication state. Completing an ended operation atomically records its known revocation duties; held-publication recovery keeps priority. Cleanup uses its own single-flight, bounded 20-record pass outside the publication queue. While a revocation is pending, only cleanup debt is deferred to the current attempt's 30-second timeout; earlier active work still wakes the Room, the deadline moves between attempts, and a restarted instance reads overdue durable debt immediately. Completion-storage failures fall through to durable retry backoff; inability to record that retry retains the original duty and continues the rest of the bounded batch.\n\nSecurity: approved. Cleanup revokes each recorded operation/attempt token ID, never an unrelated token or an inventory sweep. Expiry does not discard debt or decide publication outcome. A stopped instance checks liveness before any completion or retry write; late provider answers cannot discharge timed-out debt. No new token plaintext enters public views or the log. Provider calls in this review used local fakes only.\n\nSimplification: approved. The repair adds a cleanup deadline and an optional core scheduling floor without another durable queue, schema or Room production change. Transaction rollback preserves token flags and debt; retry handling is explicit at the per-record boundary. The remaining maximum scheduling delay of 30 seconds after a pass finishes early is documented, bounded and acceptable for this retry obligation. Full functional scope is retained.\n\nIndependent validation: fresh npm ci, root typecheck and root npm test all exit 0 on the exact clean candidate (1,992 passed, one skipped; Git Node 234, Room Node 125, Room workerd 395). Separate Git workerd 10/10 and Git-to-log 12/12 pass. Both unchanged checker reproductions now pass on actual workerd SQLite/production Room.alarm. Independently broke all 33 non-equivalent guards: M1-M20, M7b, N1-N5 and W1/W2/W3/W5/W6/W7/W9 each caused named behavioral test failures, not compilation failures. An initial broad N1 mutation run timed out; it is not counted as evidence, and N1/N3/N4 were rerun using a bounded checker control with provider-gate teardown. Additional actual-DO controls: W1/W2 reproduce immediate alarms; W9 violates the 30-second upper bound; W5/W6 reproduce missing completion-failure backoff. These five DO runs fail on the expected assertions. After source restoration, the targeted Node and both DO control sets pass again and production source matches the exact candidate. No deploy or live credentials were used.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:310d4add32d1a7b0aad91ecf0a013b42b99448e7","binding":"assigned","head":"5c2ad4f67ad26b6212b5ea28fa2c7fc25c37f145","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:51b96cc06373d681a1596a1d3a7398545672ea5c\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f38146ead8de8da66cef9454a4e77788915624e6\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6c79780f20df7ab6cfb0a745998b0ad25840d278","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}